  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## Summary\n\nValtuutus 2.3.2 fixes the tombstone reaper emptying the  table, which made every check deny after a quiet period.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- **Tombstone reaper:** transactions were pruned by age alone, so when nothing was written for longer than  the reaper deleted every row, including the newest one. The latest snap token is read from that row, so reads fell back to the oldest possible token and every check denied. No relation tuples or attributes were lost; they became invisible (#359, closes #358).\n  - Affects Postgres, SQL Server and MySQL/MariaDB. InMemory does not reap transactions.\n  - The reaper now always keeps the newest transactions row.\n\n## Upgrade notes\n\n- Anyone running  on Postgres, SQL Server or MySQL/MariaDB should upgrade.\n- If a deployment is already denying every check after a reap, upgrading alone does not bring back the deleted row. Insert one transactions row with a fresh ULID, newer than every /, or make any write:\n\n  Error:\nNo DBURL given\n\nsql [-hnr] [--table-size] [--db-size] [-p pass-through] [-s string] dburl [command]\n\n## Pull requests\n\n- #359 fix(data): keep the newest transaction when reaping",
